All 15 tests pass. Here's a summary of every bug fixed:

### `src/auth.py`
- **`has_permission`**: Added case-insensitive comparison (`required.lower() in (r.lower() for r in user_roles)`)
- **`is_admin_or_owner`**: Changed `and` to `or` — the docstring says "admin **OR** owner" but the code required both

### `src/inventory.py`
- **`__init__`**: Replaced mutable default `{}` with `None` + fresh dict creation — instances were sharing stock state
- **`add`**: Changed `self._stock[sku] = qty` to `self._stock[sku] = self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty` — was overwriting instead of accumulating
- **`reserve`**: Changed `>=` to `>` so reserving the full available amount is allowed (only over-reservation should raise `OutOfStock`)
- **`release`**: Added `if qty > current: raise ValueError(...)` — releasing more than reserved was silently going negative

### `src/text_utils.py`
- **`slugify`**: Lowercased each char; changed dash-collapsing strategy from `replace("--", "-")` (one pass) to tracking last character — only appends a dash when the previous char isn't already one
- **`truncate`**: Changed `text[:max_len] + suffix` to `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix` so the suffix fits within `max_len`
